---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { app, links } from '../config';
---
<Base title="Alpha & beta" description="Join the MacDigiPet Discord to follow development and register interest in alpha and beta testing. No release date has been set; testing is optional.">
  <div class="wrap narrow page">
    <p class="eyebrow">macOS · Community, alpha &amp; beta</p>
    <h1>Join the village.</h1>
    <p>Discord is where MacDigiPet grows: development updates, desktop screenshots, ideas from fellow Digimon fans, and the place where alpha and beta testers are invited. You’re welcome to join just to hang out.</p>
    <div class="row actions"><a class="btn" href={links.discord} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Join Discord</a><a class="btn alt" href="/wallpaper">Try the free wallpaper</a></div>

    <h2>Alpha first, then beta</h2>
    <p>The first alpha focuses on <strong>Digimon World 1</strong>: 122 forms, four eggs, the village, battles and optional original background music. It is being prepared for a small group of testers. A wider beta will follow once the alpha feedback is in.</p>
    <p>No release date has been set for either. Joining Discord does not mean a build is available yet; timing and details will be shared there when they’re ready.</p>

    <h2>Want to help test?</h2>
    <p>If you’ve played and completed Digimon World 1 and would like to help test care, evolution, the village and battles, you can share your interest. It’s optional: you can simply join and follow along.</p>
    <ol class="steps">
      <li>Join the Discord community using the button above.</li>
      <li>Post in <strong>#beta-interest</strong>. Include your Mac model/chip and macOS version, confirm that you completed Digimon World 1, and briefly describe your playthrough and what you’d like to help test.</li>
      <li>Follow the development updates. When a round of testing opens, the developer reviews interest and assigns the tester role manually. Testers get private download, feedback and bug-report channels.</li>
    </ol>
    <div class="notice">The completed-Digimon-World-1 requirement applies to testers only. Everyone is welcome in the community. Sharing interest does not reserve a slot or guarantee access or a release date, and donations do not guarantee or prioritise access.</div>

    <h2>What to expect from early builds</h2>
    <p>Early builds will have bugs, and that’s the point of testing them. They need macOS {app.minMacOS}; Apple silicon has been tested most. Builds are not yet notarised by Apple, so the first launch needs a right-click → Open. Saves stay on your Mac.</p>
    <p>This website does not collect your email or store a signup. Interest is handled manually in Discord, under Discord’s own account and privacy settings. Please keep personal details out of public messages.</p>

    <h2>Keep the project growing</h2>
    <p>Feedback and bug reports are the most useful thing you can give. If you’d also like to support development time and tools, a voluntary tip on <a href={links.kofi} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Ko-fi</a> or <a href={links.saweria} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Saweria</a> is always appreciated, never expected.</p>
  </div>
</Base>
